# Block Types Overview

A page is a **tree of blocks**. Each block has a type, its own content, and —
if it is a container — a `children` array serialized as JSON. The type decides
how the block renders, how Enter behaves inside it, and whether it can hold
other blocks.

## Two families

Blocks fall into two categories, defined in `blockCategories.ts`:

- **Leaf blocks** — hold text or a payload, but not other blocks. Paragraphs,
  headings, code, tables, equations, media, and the embedded `graph_view`.
- **Container blocks** — *parentable*, *enterCreatesChild*, and
  *selfRendersChildren*. They nest other blocks infinitely. Callouts and quotes
  are the canonical containers.

> [!info] What "selfRendersChildren" buys you
> A container renders its own children, so the read-only renderer must **not**
> also render them — doing both was a real double-render bug in callouts, since
> fixed. See [Callouts & Citations](callouts-and-citations.xmd).

## The catalogue

| Block | Family | Notes |
|:------|:-------|:------|
| `paragraph` | leaf | The default; plain rich text |
| `heading_1` · `heading_2` · `heading_3` | leaf | Feed the [outline rail](page-outline-and-toc-rail.xmd) |
| `bulleted_list` · `numbered_list` · `to_do` | leaf | Lists and checkboxes |
| `toggle` | container | Collapsible; can carry a heading level |
| `callout` | container | Semantic, typed, tinted |
| `quote` | container | Renders as `<blockquote>`, supports citation |
| `code` | leaf | Fenced, language-tagged |
| `table` | leaf | The `/table` block editor grid |
| `equation` | leaf | Block math (`$$…$$`) |
| `layout` | leaf | The `/canvas` / `/layout` freeform builder |
| `database_inline` | leaf | An embedded live-DB view |
| `graph_view` | leaf | The force-graph, embedded as a block |
| `media` | leaf | Image / video / audio asset |

## Rendering: two paths, one tree

The same block tree flows through two renderers, and both must understand every
type:

- `BlockEditor.tsx` — the editable path (what you type into).
- `ReadOnlyBlock.tsx` — the read-only path (previews, unfocused panes,
  published views).

> [!warning] Add a type, teach both renderers
> A new block type is defined in `types.ts` and `blockCategories.ts`, then
> rendered in **both** `BlockEditor.tsx` and `ReadOnlyBlock.tsx`. Heavy blocks
> (like `graph_view`) also register in the defer-mount predicates so they don't
> load until they scroll into view.
